A1.1	close#writesTheSettledStatus	the settled state being written before the closure — without it an item is closed and still reads on-hold
A1.2	close#writesTheSettledStatus	a person's not-planned decision recording the state a fix records
A1.3	close#keepsTheItemOpenWhenTheStateCannotBeWritten	a rejected label write exiting 0, so the caller proceeds from a state the tracker does not carry
A1.4	close#refusesAProfileThatNamesNoSettledState	a half-adapted profile being refused instead of silently recording the fix state
A1.5	update#commentOnlyReportsNoStatusWrite	the `already carries` note being printed only by a call that named a state (#182)
A1.6	close#refusesAClosureTheBaseDoesNotCarry	the ancestry check a closure's claim rests on (#715) — without it the item is closed on a commit the base branch does not carry, which is the state five items of the run of 2026-10-30 were found in
